data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** Cas9 paired with a synthetic guide RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site, and the cut enables site-specific insertion, deletion, or replacement [1][3].\n- **Natural origin:** The technique adapts bacterial immunity, where CRISPR sequences drawn from bacteriophage DNA detect and destroy matching viral DNA in later infections [2][1].\n- **Unverified applications:** Claimed uses include treating disease [4] and eliminating HIV in cell culture [5], but these sources provide only headlines, so the supporting details can't be confirmed."}

